hat are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415574 1072 #uuid "2512d16d-c375-5bf3-9c3b-0ab4d79702bf" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415574 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415575 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415570 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415575 1069 "q-95362" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415575 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415575 1071 "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415575 1072 #uuid "35756e17-7ddb-5db3-9246-f082e3b776e5" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415575 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =8,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{8} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415576 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415572 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415576 1069 "q-95349" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415576 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415576 1071 "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415576 1072 #uuid "42bc3fa3-d1ed-5eee-8e63-dbe17bc3a3c7" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415576 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415577 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415573 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415577 1069 "q-95375" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415577 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415577 1071 "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415577 1072 #uuid "9ba2e577-1f2d-586f-a5db-7d03c7c71c22" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415577 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )[(5-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-4)]-16(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +16)-16(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (4-\\lambda )(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415578 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415571 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415578 1069 "q-95378" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415578 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415578 1071 "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415578 1072 #uuid "9d417d43-c45e-500b-a5bf-a441848f66ea" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415578 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$  \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =2,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415579 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415582 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415579 1062 #uuid "12c4c78d-1201-5f3b-8360-4897312bf437" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415579 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415575 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415580 1062 #uuid "5d5c433e-0023-555a-a2d0-920150952da3" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415580 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415578 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415581 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415580 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415581 1062 #uuid "70681b4b-0f8d-5f23-9042-59cb06bbe55f" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415581 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415577 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415582 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415581 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415582 1062 #uuid "944a1de7-f0ef-562b-9fc3-c518a5f0b063" 13194139534241 17592186045417 true] [17592186415582 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415574 13194